# TEMPLATE ONLY for /opt/beebase/config/statistics.env -
# statistics-service's own production configuration. Never loaded by
# deploy.sh, Docker Compose, or the app directly (see
# docker-compose.prod.yml's env_file: entry for the `statistics-service`
# service, which reads the REAL file this template produces). Provision
# once on the EC2 host:
#   cp deploy/env-templates/statistics.env.example /opt/beebase/config/statistics.env
#   chmod 600 /opt/beebase/config/statistics.env
#
# statistics-service holds no database and no secret of its own today -
# it computes every statistic fresh, on every request, from
# apiary-service/hive-service/inspection-service/harvest-service. Every
# variable it needs (APP_ENV, LOG_LEVEL, HTTP_PORT, GOMEMLIMIT,
# REDIS_ADDR, AUTH_JWKS_URL, APIARY_SERVICE_URL, HIVE_SERVICE_URL,
# INSPECTION_SERVICE_URL, HARVEST_SERVICE_URL) is non-secret network
# topology supplied by
# docker-compose.prod.yml's `environment:` block instead (see
# requirement 11 in the deployment report). This file still has to
# exist - and be mode 0600 - because docker-compose.prod.yml's
# env_file: entry for statistics-service requires it, and because
# deploy.sh validates every one of the 7 services' files before it will
# touch the running stack, keeping the architecture uniform for the day
# statistics-service does need one.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logging (Optional)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Defaults to info when omitted.
# debug | info | warn | error (defaults to info if omitted)
#LOG_LEVEL=info
